  "name": "Growl Hound",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "Riddim growl: Square Morph one octave above a clean sine sub, 3-voice narrow unison, a one-shot Mod A (1/8, Decay) snapping the Index from narrow pulse back to square on every note, Saturate (2x oversampled at the default quality) into a note-tied Comb- that rings on every third harmonic, then an LP12 the filter envelope opens on the attack. Mod B slowly drifts Motion so repeated notes are never identical. Play: 1/8 and 1/16 call-and-response around F1-C2, mono legato; short notes bark, held notes settle into the metal comb tone. Tweak: Mod A Index amount for bite, Filter A Freq for the metal colour (it follows the note), Shaper Amt for dirt, Filter B Freq for darkness. FX: Tube drive +9 dB with a Post low-pass at 7 kHz for a hot, rounded bark, multiband squash at 60 % depth and fast time so every Comb ring speaks, an EQ low cut at 25 Hz and a -3 dB dip at 400 Hz, Dimension (size 0.4, wet low cut 150 Hz) to widen the growl above a mono sub, and an 8 % short plate. Harder hits open Filter B and every hit lands on a slightly different Index and comb. Macros: Growl sweeps the comb and the bark, Dirt pushes the saturation, Width opens the top above a mono sub and Space adds plate.",
  "category": "Bass/growl",
